# Accepted vulnerabilities — suppressed from FAILING the security scan, but still reported as a build WARNING.
# Format: one CVE ID per line; "#" starts a comment; an inline "# reason" is shown in the warning.
# Re-check on every base-image rebuild and remove the entry once the CVE is no longer reported.

# Added 2026-10-01. Ubuntu fixed this in openssl 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16, but no eclipse-temurin tag has rebuilt
# against it yet (26-jre-noble, 26-noble, 25-jre-noble and 26-jre all still ship a vulnerable openssl), so there
# is no patched base image to move to. Not exploitable here: the service speaks TLS through the JVM's own JSSE
# stack — netty-tcnative is absent from the runtime classpath, so nothing links against the OS libssl — and no
# component speaks DTLS, which is the affected protocol.
CVE-2026-84782 # DTLS-only openssl info disclosure; JVM uses JSSE, not OS libssl. Drop when the noble base rebuilds.

# Previously accepted: CVE-2026-45447 removed 2026-07-02 after the noble base rebuilt with patched openssl
